WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:39.084
(SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

2
00:00:39.085 --> 00:00:40.554
(INSECTS CHIRPING SOFTLY)

3
00:00:42.689 --> 00:00:45.691
BOY: <i>First, it came to Momma
as a snake.</i>

4
00:00:47.127 --> 00:00:48.328
(FROG CROAKS)

5
00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:50.630
<i>Then it took other forms
to torment her.</i>

6
00:00:53.368 --> 00:00:56.406
<i>But Momma
was a good little girl.</i>

7
00:00:56.407 --> 00:00:59.474
<i>She listened to her parents
and always stayed on the rope.</i>

8
00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:02.999
<i>So, the Evil couldn't
touch her outside the house.</i>

9
00:01:06.414 --> 00:01:08.120
<i>Because if the Evil touches you...</i>

10
00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:13.523
<i>it makes you do bad things.</i>

11
00:01:13.524 --> 00:01:15.325
(DRAMATIC BOOM)

12
00:01:24.638 --> 00:01:26.061
- (SHRIEKS)
- (GASPS)

13
00:01:32.144 --> 00:01:35.438
WOMAN: <i>O blessed house
of ancient wood.</i>

14
00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:39.312
Shelter to the pure and good.

15
00:01:39.313 --> 00:01:42.720
We'll keep you bright
and never roam.

16
00:01:42.721 --> 00:01:45.685
Heaven is here, within our home.

17
00:01:48.322 --> 00:01:50.318
(INSECTS CHIRPING SOFTLY)

18
00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:52.164
(FROG CROAKING)

19
00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.137
(OWL HOOTS)

20
00:02:01.441 --> 00:02:02.603
(RUSTLE)

21
00:02:04.536 --> 00:02:06.772
(FROG CONTINUES CROAKING)

22
00:02:17.216 --> 00:02:18.355
(OWL HOOTS)

23
00:02:25.524 --> 00:02:27.496
(FROG CONTINUES CROAKING)

24
00:02:43.675 --> 00:02:45.646
- (SILENCE FALLS)
- (SOFT RUSTLE)

25
00:02:48.347 --> 00:02:50.046
(CROAKING RESUMES)

26
00:02:52.925 --> 00:02:55.084
(CROAKING DEEPENS AND DISTORTS)

27
00:02:58.161 --> 00:02:59.958
(MALE VOICE GRUNTS SOFTLY)

28
00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:01.090
(GASPS)

29
00:03:03.198 --> 00:03:05.435
(LOW CROAKY GROWLING)

30
00:03:06.839 --> 00:03:08.768
(DISTORTED GROANING)

31
00:03:14.372 --> 00:03:16.347
(ROARING)

32
00:03:17.608 --> 00:03:19.581
(ROARING AND HISSING)

33
00:03:22.888 --> 00:03:24.183
(EVIL NOISES QUIETEN)

34
00:03:24.184 --> 00:03:25.851
(INSECTS CHIRPING SOFTLY)

35
00:03:26.384 --> 00:03:27.384
(DOOR OPENS)

36
00:03:39.398 --> 00:03:40.800
(CLOCK TICKING)

37
00:04:00.992 --> 00:04:02.954
(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)

38
00:04:28.682 --> 00:04:32.423
Samuel, Nolan,
10-minute warning, boys.

39
00:04:44.938 --> 00:04:46.503
Nine-minute warning, Nolan.

40
00:04:50.535 --> 00:04:53.167
(BELL JINGLING)

41
00:04:53.168 --> 00:04:56.675
<i>Momma says there's only love
inside of us.</i>

42
00:04:56.676 --> 00:04:59.109
<i>That's why the Evil
wants us so badly.</i>

43
00:05:01.614 --> 00:05:04.154
<i>He wants to destroy this love.</i>

44
00:05:04.155 --> 00:05:05.821
<i>Make us turn against each other.</i>

45
00:05:05.822 --> 00:05:06.922
(DOG WHINES)

46
00:05:06.923 --> 00:05:07.923
<i>Kill each other.</i>

47
00:05:11.627 --> 00:05:13.695
<i>Like it made the people
in the world do.</i>

48
00:05:23.872 --> 00:05:27.839
<i>All it needs is one touch,
without the rope on.</i>

49
00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.541
<i>And then, not even the house
can save you.</i>

50
00:05:31.542 --> 00:05:33.748
(SPOOKY MUSIC PLAYING)

51
00:06:50.128 --> 00:06:52.431
(SPOOKY MUSIC CONTINUES)

52
00:06:58.972 --> 00:07:00.637
(FOOTSTEPS THUDDING)

53
00:07:07.979 --> 00:07:08.979
(DOG WHINES)

54
00:07:27.593 --> 00:07:28.593
MOMMA: Get it.

55
00:07:29.969 --> 00:07:31.195
There you go.

56
00:07:32.435 --> 00:07:34.132
Frogs sang loud last night.

57
00:07:35.469 --> 00:07:36.469
Spring is coming.

58
00:07:37.108 --> 00:07:38.603
We'll be ready.

59
00:07:38.604 --> 00:07:40.006
It's a good day for a good day.

60
00:07:45.282 --> 00:07:46.777
Don't feed the dog.

61
00:07:46.778 --> 00:07:48.685
We're not
the only ones starving.

62
00:07:53.051 --> 00:07:54.889
And I don't need to eat
as much as you.

63
00:08:00.492 --> 00:08:01.492
Momma?

64
00:08:02.632 --> 00:08:04.996
Momma, can we listen
to it tonight?

65
00:08:04.997 --> 00:08:07.002
- SAMUEL: It's not new moon.
- I'm asking Momma.

66
00:08:07.003 --> 00:08:08.600
We should wait.

67
00:08:08.601 --> 00:08:10.170
It won't be special if we don't.

68
00:08:10.171 --> 00:08:11.510
SAMUEL: Told ya.

69
00:08:14.508 --> 00:08:15.745
(NOLAN GRUNTING)

70
00:08:20.745 --> 00:08:21.850
(NOLAN SIGHS)

71
00:08:24.849 --> 00:08:26.382
You'll grow into 'em.

72
00:08:54.053 --> 00:08:55.686
(ROPES CREAK)

73
00:08:57.016 --> 00:08:59.420
ALL: The Evil
can't touch me here,

74
00:08:59.421 --> 00:09:01.522
dawn to night and year to year.

75
00:09:01.523 --> 00:09:04.152
The forest
with its dangers abound,

76
00:09:04.153 --> 00:09:06.862
wrapped up tight
and safe and sound.

77
00:09:27.954 --> 00:09:29.115
(DOG WHINES)

78
00:09:35.118 --> 00:09:37.420
(SLOW SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

79
00:09:43.729 --> 00:09:44.729
Do you see it?

80
00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:01.785
Go get 'em, Koda.
Bring us a big, fat rabbit.

81
00:10:05.653 --> 00:10:06.823
MOMMA: Y'all ready?

82
00:10:11.658 --> 00:10:12.994
Never let go.

83
00:10:14.496 --> 00:10:15.832
Never let go.

84
00:10:19.802 --> 00:10:22.168
(SLOW SUSPENSEFUL
MUSIC CONTINUES)

85
00:10:56.142 --> 00:10:58.336
(FROG CROAKING)

86
00:11:07.011 --> 00:11:08.984
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYS)

87
00:11:17.394 --> 00:11:20.197
(METAL SQUEAKING)

88
00:11:20.198 --> 00:11:21.556
SAMUEL: <i>Momma told us</i>

89
00:11:21.557 --> 00:11:23.630
<i>that even before the Evil
possessed everyone,</i>

90
00:11:23.631 --> 00:11:25.495
<i>the world was already bad.</i>

91
00:11:26.932 --> 00:11:28.131
<i>And that's why it came.</i>

92
00:11:28.132 --> 00:11:29.702
<i>The people opened
their door for it,</i>

93
00:11:29.703 --> 00:11:31.237
<i>whether they knew it or not.</i>

94
00:11:35.405 --> 00:11:36.847
WHISPERING MALE VOICE:
Let them go.

95
00:11:40.177 --> 00:11:42.081
SAMUEL: <i>But Grandma knew it.</i>

96
00:11:42.082 --> 00:11:44.382
<i>And Grandpa was the only one
to believe her.</i>

97
00:11:49.356 --> 00:11:52.655
<i>He was a good man
and built this place for her.</i>

98
00:11:52.656 --> 00:11:55.591
<i>A blessed house where the Evil
wouldn't be able to come in.</i>

99
00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:58.228
<i>A place to raise a family,</i>

100
00:11:58.229 --> 00:12:00.431
<i>far away from the darkness
of the world.</i>

101
00:12:04.277 --> 00:12:06.041
<i>It was a good life.</i>

102
00:12:06.042 --> 00:12:08.674
<i>But after a while, Grandma
started to feel a presence</i>

103
00:12:08.675 --> 00:12:10.078
<i>lurking in the woods.</i>

104
00:12:10.942 --> 00:12:12.113
<i>Something evil,</i>

105
00:12:12.813 --> 00:12:14.442
<i>getting stronger.</i>

106
00:12:14.443 --> 00:12:17.082
<i>She refused to leave
the house anymore.</i>

107
00:12:17.083 --> 00:12:19.081
<i>So, Grandpa figured out
how to tie a rope</i>

108
00:12:19.082 --> 00:12:21.085
<i>to the foundation of the house,</i>

109
00:12:21.086 --> 00:12:23.058
<i>so she could finally go outside.</i>

110
00:12:24.396 --> 00:12:26.622
(CRYPTIC MUSIC PLAYS)

111
00:12:28.793 --> 00:12:30.098
(GRUNTS)

112
00:12:32.568 --> 00:12:34.069
(HEAVY BREATH)

113
00:12:34.768 --> 00:12:36.335
(LEAVES RUSTLING)

114
00:12:38.602 --> 00:12:41.406
WHISPERING MALE VOICE:
Let them go, Junebug.

115
00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:46.479
(CROW CAWS)

116
00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:47.852
(SQUEAKING)

117
00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.295
(SOFT THUD)

118
00:13:04.636 --> 00:13:06.035
- (GRUNTS)
- (FLESH SQUELCHES)

119
00:13:09.702 --> 00:13:10.875
Whoo!

120
00:13:11.375 --> 00:13:13.674
Whoo-hoo!

121
00:13:13.675 --> 00:13:15.979
(LIGHT-HEARTED MUSIC PLAYING)

122
00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:48.209
(CROAKING)

123
00:14:05.693 --> 00:14:06.723
(CRUNCHES)

124
00:14:06.724 --> 00:14:08.229
(GRUNTING)

125
00:14:30.585 --> 00:14:31.585
(GRUNTS)

126
00:14:47.606 --> 00:14:48.940
- (ROPE THUDS)
- (GRUNTS)

127
00:14:53.311 --> 00:14:55.045
(GRUNTS)

128
00:15:00.582 --> 00:15:01.645
(GRUNTS)

129
00:15:09.954 --> 00:15:10.954
Nolan.

130
00:15:12.498 --> 00:15:13.929
What are you doing?

131
00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.056
Making some slack
so I can grab this egg.

132
00:15:16.057 --> 00:15:17.232
Don't.

133
00:15:19.097 --> 00:15:20.395
Could be a trick.

134
00:15:20.396 --> 00:15:22.571
I could grab it.
It's right there.

135
00:15:22.572 --> 00:15:24.030
Give me your machete.

136
00:15:24.031 --> 00:15:25.031
No.

137
00:15:26.941 --> 00:15:28.303
We'll let Momma decide.

138
00:15:28.304 --> 00:15:30.245
She can tie the ropes together.

139
00:15:32.814 --> 00:15:34.084
(BLOWS SOFTLY)

140
00:15:44.464 --> 00:15:45.854
I wasn't gonna let go.

141
00:15:47.329 --> 00:15:49.799
We didn't get this far
just to die of hunger.

142
00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:51.768
How can you be so sure
of everything?

143
00:15:51.769 --> 00:15:53.262
SAMUEL: Because
I'm older than you.

144
00:15:53.263 --> 00:15:55.435
NOLAN: Yeah. By three minutes.

145
00:16:02.780 --> 00:16:03.872
SAMUEL: She loves me more.

146
00:16:04.448 --> 00:16:05.448
What?

147
00:16:07.143 --> 00:16:08.143
What?

148
00:16:08.685 --> 00:16:09.812
What did you say?

149
00:16:12.283 --> 00:16:13.523
I didn't say anything.

150
00:16:13.524 --> 00:16:15.356
(UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING)

151
00:16:25.162 --> 00:16:26.730
(GRUNTING)

152
00:16:28.505 --> 00:16:29.505
Sam!

153
00:16:30.907 --> 00:16:32.835
- (BONES CRACK)
- (GROANS)

154
00:16:32.836 --> 00:16:33.937
Sam!

155
00:16:33.938 --> 00:16:35.504
(BLOWS WHISTLE)

156
00:16:35.505 --> 00:16:37.906
- (WHISTLE BLOWING IN DISTANCE)
- (GASPS)

157
00:16:39.318 --> 00:16:40.348
Sam!

158
00:16:41.013 --> 00:16:42.482
(GRUNTING)

159
00:16:45.425 --> 00:16:46.519
MOMMA: Nolan!

160
00:16:47.018 --> 00:16:48.059
Samuel!

161
00:16:49.087 --> 00:16:51.062
(GROANING)

162
00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:53.893
NOLAN: Sam!

163
00:16:53.894 --> 00:16:55.891
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

164
00:16:57.193 --> 00:16:58.432
My rope.

165
00:17:01.738 --> 00:17:03.297
(FOOTSTEPS RUSTLE)

166
00:17:03.298 --> 00:17:04.834
(SOFT SQUELCHING)

167
00:17:07.611 --> 00:17:09.003
(RATTLING)

168
00:17:09.942 --> 00:17:11.647
Samuel!

169
00:17:11.648 --> 00:17:13.612
(RATTLING GROWING LOUDER)

170
00:17:14.685 --> 00:17:16.384
(LOUD BREATH)

171
00:17:16.385 --> 00:17:17.616
Sam!

172
00:17:18.588 --> 00:17:20.058
Sam!

173
00:17:22.295 --> 00:17:23.559
Samuel!

174
00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.591
- Samuel!
- Sam! Sam.

175
00:17:28.525 --> 00:17:30.200
- Come on.
- (SAMUEL GROANS)

176
00:17:32.195 --> 00:17:33.195
Nolan!

177
00:17:33.867 --> 00:17:34.901
Run!

178
00:17:34.902 --> 00:17:36.635
Get back on the rope!

179
00:17:44.208 --> 00:17:45.545
(GROWLING)

180
00:17:46.717 --> 00:17:48.508
(SAMUEL GRUNTING)

181
00:17:48.509 --> 00:17:50.484
(SNARLING AND HISSING)

182
00:17:59.597 --> 00:18:02.091
No! No. No!

183
00:18:02.092 --> 00:18:04.135
No! No! No!

184
00:18:11.344 --> 00:18:12.344
Okay.

185
00:18:18.676 --> 00:18:21.409
- (MOMMA GASPING)
- (SAMUEL GROANING)

186
00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:23.253
Did it touch you? Huh?

187
00:18:24.352 --> 00:18:26.314
- Uh-uh.
- Did it touch you, Nolan?

188
00:18:26.315 --> 00:18:27.752
I don't think so.

189
00:18:28.592 --> 00:18:29.754
(GROWLS)

190
00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:32.760
(HISSES)

191
00:18:34.195 --> 00:18:35.463
MOMMA: Hold on to the rope.

192
00:18:39.929 --> 00:18:41.899
NOLAN: What do you see?
Momma, what is it?

193
00:18:41.900 --> 00:18:43.306
(HISSING)

194
00:18:45.545 --> 00:18:46.545
(HISSING STOPS)

195
00:18:47.438 --> 00:18:49.645
Breathe. Just breathe.

196
00:18:49.646 --> 00:18:51.149
(SAMUEL WHIMPERING)

197
00:18:52.546 --> 00:18:55.278
- (CHITTERING AND HISSING)
- (WHIMPERING)

198
00:18:55.279 --> 00:18:56.443
(EVIL NOISES QUIETEN)

199
00:18:56.444 --> 00:18:58.815
Breathe. Breathe.

200
00:18:58.816 --> 00:19:02.183
It's okay. It's okay.
Just breathe. Just breathe.

201
00:19:02.184 --> 00:19:03.691
(PANTING)

202
00:19:03.692 --> 00:19:04.692
Just breathe.

203
00:19:05.523 --> 00:19:07.363
(SAMUEL GRUNTING IN PAIN)

204
00:19:10.901 --> 00:19:12.261
MOMMA: On your knees.

205
00:19:12.262 --> 00:19:13.336
I need to be sure.

206
00:19:15.872 --> 00:19:17.034
Don't look at me.

207
00:19:17.035 --> 00:19:18.531
Touch the wood!

208
00:19:18.532 --> 00:19:19.837
Hands on the cellar.

209
00:19:20.369 --> 00:19:21.369
Say it.

210
00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.080
Say it!

211
00:19:30.319 --> 00:19:34.153
BOTH: O blessed house
of ancient wood.

212
00:19:34.154 --> 00:19:36.784
Shelter to the pure and good.

213
00:19:36.785 --> 00:19:39.727
We'll keep you bright
and never roam.

214
00:19:39.728 --> 00:19:41.487
Heaven is here,

215
00:19:41.488 --> 00:19:42.992
within our home.

216
00:19:50.434 --> 00:19:51.434
Okay, get up.

217
00:19:52.875 --> 00:19:54.168
(GRUNTING)

218
00:19:55.345 --> 00:19:57.538
- What happened?
- NOLAN: I didn't mean to.

219
00:19:57.539 --> 00:19:58.715
I stepped on his rope...

220
00:19:58.716 --> 00:20:01.050
Have you lost your mind?

221
00:20:01.051 --> 00:20:02.483
It's all right, Momma.
He didn't...

222
00:20:02.484 --> 00:20:06.479
Quiet! One more second
and it woulda all been over.

223
00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:08.088
For all of us!

224
00:20:08.089 --> 00:20:10.820
That rope is your lifeline.

225
00:20:10.821 --> 00:20:12.994
- NOLAN: I'm sorry.
- I don't need you to be sorry!

226
00:20:12.995 --> 00:20:14.628
I need you to use your head!

227
00:20:15.294 --> 00:20:17.092
(CRYING IN PAIN)

228
00:20:28.648 --> 00:20:29.648
Can you move it?

229
00:20:30.573 --> 00:20:31.747
(SAMUEL GRUNTS)

230
00:20:31.748 --> 00:20:32.976
I think it's broke.

231
00:20:43.626 --> 00:20:46.660
Don't just stand there.
Get me a splint for his ankle.

232
00:20:50.563 --> 00:20:53.227
- (CRIES)
- I know. I know, I know.

233
00:20:55.808 --> 00:20:57.099
Come on. It's okay.

234
00:21:02.475 --> 00:21:04.612
What'd it look like this time?

235
00:21:10.514 --> 00:21:11.514
Like my momma.

236
00:21:15.421 --> 00:21:16.756
It's trying to scare me.

237
00:21:18.791 --> 00:21:21.299
<i>Like it tried to scare
my momma before.</i>

238
00:21:32.009 --> 00:21:33.971
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYS)

239
00:21:49.552 --> 00:21:50.856
(SLITHERING)

240
00:21:51.697 --> 00:21:53.023
(SQUELCHING)

241
00:22:07.405 --> 00:22:08.808
(SIZZLING)

242
00:22:16.218 --> 00:22:17.751
That's all we got today.

243
00:22:20.024 --> 00:22:21.359
Don't eat too fast.

244
00:22:23.895 --> 00:22:25.055
Sure is good.

245
00:22:42.278 --> 00:22:44.808
MOMMA: I used to be thankful

246
00:22:44.809 --> 00:22:47.275
that the Evil
didn't show itself to you.

247
00:22:51.114 --> 00:22:54.458
And then, I figured out
what it was doing.

248
00:22:58.557 --> 00:23:00.189
I never told y'all this.

249
00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:02.191
But one time,

250
00:23:03.233 --> 00:23:05.293
it came to me as a little girl,

251
00:23:06.367 --> 00:23:07.735
crying out for help.

252
00:23:09.932 --> 00:23:13.037
She was just at my rope's limit.

253
00:23:15.281 --> 00:23:18.306
She got her foot stuck
in a gopher hole.

254
00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:23.346
She was howling, screaming.

255
00:23:23.347 --> 00:23:24.455
(SCREAMING)

256
00:23:25.748 --> 00:23:27.216
I saw the bone

257
00:23:28.157 --> 00:23:30.954
sticking out.

258
00:23:30.955 --> 00:23:34.262
I had to keep telling myself
that it wasn't real.

259
00:23:34.263 --> 00:23:36.995
But the screams
went on for days.

260
00:23:38.167 --> 00:23:39.602
So, every morning,

261
00:23:40.335 --> 00:23:41.901
I went out to check...

262
00:23:43.966 --> 00:23:45.509
to see if the Evil had given up.

263
00:23:48.475 --> 00:23:50.871
But she was still there.

264
00:23:50.872 --> 00:23:53.946
Her skin turned blue and gray.

265
00:23:57.317 --> 00:23:58.317
The smell...

266
00:24:01.019 --> 00:24:03.494
I wondered
why she was still out there.

267
00:24:04.356 --> 00:24:06.429
Why?

268
00:24:06.430 --> 00:24:09.027
Because it wanted me
to go see about that girl.

269
00:24:10.366 --> 00:24:12.470
It wanted me to doubt myself.

270
00:24:13.368 --> 00:24:15.506
To lure me off the rope.

271
00:24:16.437 --> 00:24:17.970
The Evil is clever...

272
00:24:19.636 --> 00:24:22.170
and patient.

273
00:24:22.171 --> 00:24:25.477
It's like the snake
you've seen in the woods.

274
00:24:25.478 --> 00:24:29.179
Evil can wear many, many skins.

275
00:24:31.618 --> 00:24:33.821
And the greatest trick of all,

276
00:24:34.621 --> 00:24:36.384
it's playing on you boys.

277
00:24:37.294 --> 00:24:39.691
And when enough time goes by,

278
00:24:39.692 --> 00:24:41.829
you're gonna forget
it's even there.

279
00:24:42.961 --> 00:24:44.865
You're gonna
let your guard down.

280
00:24:45.664 --> 00:24:46.967
And it's gonna get you!

281
00:24:46.968 --> 00:24:47.968
(GASPS)

282
00:24:50.810 --> 00:24:52.367
One touch

283
00:24:53.704 --> 00:24:55.370
without a rope on

284
00:24:56.982 --> 00:24:58.541
is all it takes

285
00:24:58.542 --> 00:25:00.874
to possess one of us

286
00:25:00.875 --> 00:25:02.751
and get inside the house.

287
00:25:03.679 --> 00:25:04.852
Never

288
00:25:06.055 --> 00:25:07.316
let go.

289
00:25:09.687 --> 00:25:11.023
Never let go.

290
00:25:13.999 --> 00:25:15.225
(DOOR CREAKS)

291
00:25:18.203 --> 00:25:20.362
(LOW EERIE MUSIC PLAYING)

292
00:25:26.375 --> 00:25:28.337
(CREAKING CONTINUES)

293
00:25:36.548 --> 00:25:37.548
How long?

294
00:25:38.717 --> 00:25:39.887
MOMMA: About an hour.

295
00:25:40.851 --> 00:25:42.585
Felt longer tonight.

296
00:25:42.586 --> 00:25:43.924
Did you imagine it?

297
00:25:48.592 --> 00:25:49.592
Yes.

298
00:25:52.400 --> 00:25:54.670
Tell us about it.

299
00:25:54.671 --> 00:25:57.696
- I imagined it was all gone.
- (GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING)

300
00:25:57.697 --> 00:25:58.708
You.

301
00:26:00.439 --> 00:26:01.439
Sam.

302
00:26:02.771 --> 00:26:03.771
Koda.

303
00:26:05.247 --> 00:26:06.247
The house.

304
00:26:08.880 --> 00:26:10.984
All I had left was the darkness.

305
00:26:11.782 --> 00:26:12.953
And then what?

306
00:26:14.559 --> 00:26:17.019
I thought about our birth
in the house,

307
00:26:17.020 --> 00:26:19.955
and how safe
it keeps us every day.

308
00:26:19.956 --> 00:26:21.731
And I felt
the darkness float away.

309
00:26:22.935 --> 00:26:24.129
Look around.

310
00:26:25.896 --> 00:26:27.862
Look how lucky you are.

311
00:26:27.863 --> 00:26:30.800
All your dreams came true.

312
00:26:30.801 --> 00:26:32.676
The Evil can't touch you here.

313
00:26:34.343 --> 00:26:36.772
Samuel, your turn.

314
00:26:36.773 --> 00:26:38.440
Time to clean your soul.

315
00:26:43.953 --> 00:26:48.083
Remember, lose us completely
and then find us again.

316
00:26:48.084 --> 00:26:50.990
Fill the cellar up
with all your love.

317
00:26:50.991 --> 00:26:54.291
You remind the house
why we deserve its protection.

318
00:26:59.296 --> 00:27:01.630
- (CELLAR DOOR SLAMS)
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)

319
00:27:01.631 --> 00:27:03.300
(RAIN PATTERING)

320
00:27:05.969 --> 00:27:07.172
SAMUEL: Can I move yet?

321
00:27:07.771 --> 00:27:09.168
NOLAN: Nope.

322
00:27:09.169 --> 00:27:11.071
SAMUEL: Nolan, I got an itch.

323
00:27:11.072 --> 00:27:13.249
NOLAN: I said, "Don't move."

324
00:27:13.250 --> 00:27:14.476
SAMUEL: It's just one itch.

325
00:27:16.845 --> 00:27:17.845
Okay.

326
00:27:19.883 --> 00:27:20.889
That should do it.

327
00:27:25.624 --> 00:27:26.624
SAMUEL: Wow.

328
00:27:27.496 --> 00:27:29.030
Are those owl wings?

329
00:27:29.031 --> 00:27:30.031
Uh-huh.

330
00:27:31.567 --> 00:27:33.125
I can fly anywhere I want.

331
00:27:33.126 --> 00:27:34.837
And eat whatever you want.

332
00:27:36.207 --> 00:27:37.768
Once upon a time,

333
00:27:37.769 --> 00:27:39.839
there was a boy who could fly

334
00:27:39.840 --> 00:27:42.075
and catch all the squirrels
in the trees.

335
00:27:45.512 --> 00:27:47.542
(HOOTING)

336
00:27:50.582 --> 00:27:52.019
(LAUGHS)

337
00:28:01.033 --> 00:28:02.033
Hey, Sam.

338
00:28:03.367 --> 00:28:04.768
After your rope broke,

339
00:28:05.600 --> 00:28:06.836
did you notice anything?

340
00:28:08.502 --> 00:28:09.666
Like what?

341
00:28:09.667 --> 00:28:11.397
Anything strange.

342
00:28:11.398 --> 00:28:13.568
That was the first time
we ever let go.

343
00:28:15.709 --> 00:28:17.378
And nothing changed.

344
00:28:17.379 --> 00:28:18.672
'Cause it didn't get us.

345
00:28:20.216 --> 00:28:21.216
Yeah.

346
00:28:28.116 --> 00:28:30.152
NOLAN: If it did,

347
00:28:30.153 --> 00:28:32.389
do you think
Momma woulda killed us?

348
00:28:34.629 --> 00:28:35.898
Like she killed Poppa?

349
00:28:39.065 --> 00:28:41.369
Like she killed
Grandma and Grandpa?

350
00:28:41.370 --> 00:28:42.905
The Evil touched them.

351
00:28:43.968 --> 00:28:45.402
She was protecting us.

352
00:28:46.034 --> 00:28:47.034
I know that.

353
00:28:53.711 --> 00:28:54.907
What?

354
00:28:54.908 --> 00:28:55.918
Nothing.

355
00:29:00.957 --> 00:29:02.850
You ever wish
you could run free like Koda?

356
00:29:02.851 --> 00:29:03.921
(KODA WHINES)

357
00:29:03.922 --> 00:29:05.227
Without a rope
around your chest?

358
00:29:05.228 --> 00:29:07.090
But Koda's a dog.

359
00:29:07.091 --> 00:29:09.228
The Evil doesn't care
about animals.

360
00:29:26.751 --> 00:29:28.918
You ever wish you could see
what she sees?

361
00:29:29.583 --> 00:29:30.854
Just once?

362
00:29:33.658 --> 00:29:36.354
I felt something
getting closer today.

363
00:29:37.186 --> 00:29:38.521
You were just scared.

364
00:29:41.524 --> 00:29:43.262
Why are you asking
all these questions?

365
00:29:44.501 --> 00:29:46.298
Momma never lied to us.

366
00:29:53.005 --> 00:29:55.043
(THUNDER CONTINUES RUMBLING)

367
00:29:56.711 --> 00:29:58.112
"She loves me more."

368
00:30:00.711 --> 00:30:03.648
That's what I heard you say
before I stepped on your rope.

369
00:30:03.649 --> 00:30:04.778
I didn't say that.

370
00:30:10.957 --> 00:30:12.390
I didn't mean for what happened.

371
00:30:14.561 --> 00:30:15.723
I know.

372
00:30:23.968 --> 00:30:26.074
(SOFT SCRAPING)

373
00:30:28.577 --> 00:30:30.940
(CHAIR CREAKING)

374
00:30:30.941 --> 00:30:32.707
(INSECTS CHIRPING SOFTLY)

375
00:30:48.224 --> 00:30:49.592
(CHAIR STOPS CREAKING)

376
00:31:05.075 --> 00:31:06.745
(SOFT FOOTSTEPS)

377
00:31:06.746 --> 00:31:08.215
MAN: O blessed house...

378
00:31:11.752 --> 00:31:13.055
of ancient wood.

379
00:31:14.687 --> 00:31:15.687
Home...

380
00:31:16.956 --> 00:31:18.423
to my runaway wife.

381
00:31:27.966 --> 00:31:29.302
Hey, Junebug.

382
00:31:33.444 --> 00:31:34.444
What's wrong?

383
00:31:37.215 --> 00:31:38.215
June!

384
00:31:39.580 --> 00:31:40.580
June!

385
00:31:43.553 --> 00:31:44.614
June, it's me.

386
00:31:50.395 --> 00:31:51.456
It's been a while.

387
00:31:53.630 --> 00:31:55.064
God, have I missed you.

388
00:31:57.161 --> 00:31:58.430
You think I can see 'em?

389
00:32:03.734 --> 00:32:06.009
Oh, you ain't told 'em
the truth about their father.

390
00:32:07.675 --> 00:32:08.675
I get it.

391
00:32:10.279 --> 00:32:12.411
'Cause then you got to
tell 'em who you really are.

392
00:32:13.675 --> 00:32:15.945
Ain't that right,
my little Junebug?

393
00:32:15.946 --> 00:32:17.350
I'm not her no more.

394
00:32:18.248 --> 00:32:19.484
You know you loved it.

395
00:32:21.921 --> 00:32:22.960
What's your plan?

396
00:32:23.823 --> 00:32:25.461
I know ya.

397
00:32:25.462 --> 00:32:26.689
You ain't got no plan.

398
00:32:27.766 --> 00:32:29.798
You might as well
give 'em to me.

399
00:32:29.799 --> 00:32:31.661
Or would you rather
watch them starve?

400
00:32:38.301 --> 00:32:40.175
I came so close today.

401
00:32:46.649 --> 00:32:47.649
Sooner or later,

402
00:32:49.048 --> 00:32:50.218
you're gonna let go.

403
00:32:51.555 --> 00:32:52.715
And when you do...

404
00:32:58.129 --> 00:33:00.525
(DISTORTED) I'm gonna
make you eat your babies.

405
00:33:02.465 --> 00:33:03.465
June!

406
00:33:04.192 --> 00:33:05.192
June!

407
00:33:13.339 --> 00:33:15.408
Careful now.
Don't break those roots.

408
00:33:20.916 --> 00:33:22.250
You think it'll get better?

409
00:33:23.082 --> 00:33:24.884
MOMMA: Hard to say.

410
00:33:24.885 --> 00:33:27.116
The winter did a number on us.

411
00:33:27.117 --> 00:33:29.092
All we can do now is hope.

412
00:33:32.220 --> 00:33:33.228
What?

413
00:33:33.661 --> 00:33:34.661
Nothing.

414
00:33:40.704 --> 00:33:43.170
The snake on your back.

415
00:33:43.171 --> 00:33:46.536
You said you got it
when you were in the city.

416
00:33:46.537 --> 00:33:49.236
But you also said
the Evil was already there,

417
00:33:49.237 --> 00:33:50.542
killing everybody.

418
00:33:51.506 --> 00:33:52.538
I don't understand...

419
00:33:52.539 --> 00:33:54.051
I got it before it all started.

420
00:33:55.851 --> 00:33:57.186
When I met your Poppa.

421
00:33:58.384 --> 00:34:00.420
I was a different person
back then.

422
00:34:01.285 --> 00:34:02.285
Does it still scare you?

423
00:34:03.593 --> 00:34:05.251
Not anymore.

424
00:34:05.252 --> 00:34:06.261
I like it now.

425
00:34:07.959 --> 00:34:09.525
Why?

426
00:34:09.526 --> 00:34:11.398
NOLAN: Because
it's from your life before.

427
00:34:12.603 --> 00:34:14.728
In the old world.

428
00:34:14.729 --> 00:34:16.964
MOMMA: A world
full of pain and suffering?

429
00:34:17.907 --> 00:34:19.406
What's to like about that?

430
00:34:22.710 --> 00:34:23.710
Huh?

431
00:34:24.482 --> 00:34:25.482
Don't know.

432
00:34:26.211 --> 00:34:27.645
When I was your age,

433
00:34:29.050 --> 00:34:30.978
asking questions like you do,

434
00:34:32.452 --> 00:34:34.223
I didn't really believe
my momma, either.

435
00:34:35.255 --> 00:34:37.750
- That's why you left?
- Mm-hmm.

436
00:34:37.751 --> 00:34:39.558
Never thought
I'd come back here.

437
00:34:41.099 --> 00:34:44.425
But it's the only place
I could keep y'all safe.

438
00:34:44.426 --> 00:34:46.396
But what if the Evil did...

439
00:34:46.397 --> 00:34:47.896
touch one of us
and come in the house?

440
00:34:48.804 --> 00:34:49.997
What would happen?

441
00:34:51.942 --> 00:34:54.534
It would make us
kill each other.

442
00:34:54.535 --> 00:34:56.069
That's how the world ended.

443
00:35:02.248 --> 00:35:04.582
But how do you know we're alone?

444
00:35:04.583 --> 00:35:07.481
Maybe our house isn't
the only one that's protected.

445
00:35:07.482 --> 00:35:09.751
Would that make you feel better?

446
00:35:09.752 --> 00:35:11.627
We wouldn't be alone
for the rest of our lives.

447
00:35:11.628 --> 00:35:13.727
We're not alone, Nolan.

448
00:35:13.728 --> 00:35:15.132
We have each other.

449
00:35:15.832 --> 00:35:17.134
And that's everything.

450
00:35:19.036 --> 00:35:21.303
There's nobody else
out there, baby.

451
00:35:23.433 --> 00:35:24.834
We're the world now.

452
00:35:25.534 --> 00:35:27.507
(DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING)

453
00:35:41.693 --> 00:35:43.187
<i>"Once upon a time,</i>

454
00:35:43.188 --> 00:35:45.121
"there dwelt near a large wood

455
00:35:45.122 --> 00:35:46.929
"a poor woodcutter,

456
00:35:46.930 --> 00:35:48.957
<i>"with his wife
and two children..."</i>

457
00:35:51.363 --> 00:35:53.428
<i>"a little boy called Hansel</i>

458
00:35:53.429 --> 00:35:55.303
<i>"and a girl called Gretel.</i>

459
00:35:55.304 --> 00:35:58.767
<i>"Once, when there was
a great famine in the land,"</i>

460
00:35:58.768 --> 00:36:01.201
<i>"he could not procure
even his daily bread."</i>

461
00:36:01.202 --> 00:36:02.540
(WINCES)

462
00:36:02.541 --> 00:36:05.704
"As he lay there thinking
in the bed one evening,

463
00:36:05.705 --> 00:36:07.382
"rolling about for trouble,"

464
00:36:09.251 --> 00:36:11.012
<i>"he sighed and said to his wife,</i>

465
00:36:12.186 --> 00:36:14.356
<i>"'What will become of us?"</i>

466
00:36:15.992 --> 00:36:18.986
"'How will I feed my children

467
00:36:18.987 --> 00:36:23.725
<i>"'when we have no more
that we can eat ourselves?'</i>

468
00:36:23.726 --> 00:36:26.560
<i>"'Know, then, my husband, '
answered she, </i>

469
00:36:26.561 --> 00:36:27.831
<i>"'we will lead them away,"</i>

470
00:36:29.765 --> 00:36:32.173
<i>"'quite early in the morning,</i>

471
00:36:32.174 --> 00:36:34.101
<i>"'into the thickest part
of the woods.</i>

472
00:36:35.539 --> 00:36:37.839
<i>"'And there make them a fire"</i>

473
00:36:37.840 --> 00:36:40.581
"'and give them each
a little piece of bread.'"

474
00:36:40.582 --> 00:36:41.779
(GRUNTING)

475
00:36:44.055 --> 00:36:46.220
<i>"'And then
we will go to our work</i>

476
00:36:46.221 --> 00:36:48.321
<i>- "'and leave them alone.'"</i>
- (KODA WHINES)

477
00:36:48.322 --> 00:36:50.755
<i>"'They will not find
a way home again."</i>

478
00:36:52.196 --> 00:36:54.858
<i>"'And we shall be freed
from them.'"</i>

479
00:37:11.474 --> 00:37:12.604
NOLAN: It's new.

480
00:37:12.605 --> 00:37:14.112
SAMUEL: You sure?

481
00:37:14.113 --> 00:37:15.483
You got eyes, don't you?

482
00:37:16.248 --> 00:37:17.685
It's a new moon.

483
00:37:17.686 --> 00:37:18.686
Right, Momma?

484
00:37:19.748 --> 00:37:21.214
Can we listen to it tonight?

485
00:37:29.599 --> 00:37:32.401
<i>(THE BIG ROCK CANDY MOUNTAIN</i>
BY HARRY MCCLINTOCK PLAYING)

486
00:37:35.273 --> 00:37:38.404
<i>♪ One evening
as the sun went down ♪</i>

487
00:37:38.405 --> 00:37:41.100
<i>♪ And the jungle fire
was burning ♪</i>

488
00:37:41.101 --> 00:37:43.541
<i>♪ Down the track
came a hobo hikin' ♪</i>

489
00:37:43.542 --> 00:37:46.476
<i>♪ He said,
"Boys, I'm not turning ♪</i>

490
00:37:46.477 --> 00:37:47.908
<i>♪ "I'm headed for a land ♪</i>

491
00:37:47.909 --> 00:37:49.249
<i>- ♪ That's far away ♪</i>
- (KODA WHINES)

492
00:37:49.250 --> 00:37:51.744
<i>"♪ "Beside
the crystal fountains ♪</i>

493
00:37:51.745 --> 00:37:52.979
<i>♪ "So come with me ♪</i>

494
00:37:52.980 --> 00:37:54.882
<i>- ♪ "We'll go and see" ♪</i>
- Come on, Momma.

495
00:37:54.883 --> 00:37:57.324
<i>♪ "The Big Rock
Candy Mountains" ♪</i>

496
00:37:57.325 --> 00:37:59.955
<i>♪ In the Big Rock
Candy Mountains ♪</i>

497
00:37:59.956 --> 00:38:02.594
<i>♪ There's a land
that's fair and bright ♪</i>

498
00:38:02.595 --> 00:38:05.167
<i>♪ Where the handouts
grow on bushes ♪</i>

499
00:38:05.168 --> 00:38:07.763
<i>♪ And you sleep out
every night ♪</i>

500
00:38:07.764 --> 00:38:10.502
<i>♪ Where the boxcars
all are empty ♪</i>

501
00:38:10.503 --> 00:38:12.937
<i>♪ And the sun shines
every day ♪</i>

502
00:38:12.938 --> 00:38:15.742
<i>♪ On the birds and the bees
And the cigarette trees ♪</i>

503
00:38:15.743 --> 00:38:18.345
<i>♪ And the lemonade springs
Where the bluebird sings ♪</i>

504
00:38:18.346 --> 00:38:20.713
<i>♪ In the Big Rock
Candy Mountains ♪</i>

505
00:38:21.978 --> 00:38:24.681
<i>♪ In the Big Rock
Candy Mountains ♪</i>

506
00:38:24.682 --> 00:38:27.147
<i>♪ All the cops
have wooden legs ♪</i>

507
00:38:27.148 --> 00:38:29.785
<i>♪ And the bulldogs
all have rubber teeth ♪</i>

508
00:38:29.786 --> 00:38:32.284
<i>♪ And the hens
lay soft-boiled eggs ♪</i>

509
00:38:32.285 --> 00:38:34.955
<i>♪ And the farmers' trees
are full of fruit ♪</i>

510
00:38:34.956 --> 00:38:37.323
<i>♪ And the barns
are full of hay ♪</i>

511
00:38:37.324 --> 00:38:39.931
<i>♪ Oh I'm bound to go
where there ain't no snow ♪</i>

512
00:38:39.932 --> 00:38:42.666
<i>♪ Where the rain don't fall
And the wind don't blow ♪</i>

513
00:38:42.667 --> 00:38:45.168
<i>♪ In the Big Rock
Candy Mountains ♪</i>

514
00:38:45.169 --> 00:38:46.270
(SONG FADES OUT)

515
00:38:46.271 --> 00:38:48.235
(OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

516
00:38:48.879 --> 00:38:50.743
(RAIN PATTERING)

517
00:38:52.711 --> 00:38:54.142
- (THUNDER RUMBLES)
- (MUSIC FADES)

518
00:39:30.353 --> 00:39:32.918
- (FLOOR CREAKS)
- (OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING)

519
00:39:32.919 --> 00:39:33.919
(GASPS)

520
00:39:36.586 --> 00:39:37.724
MOMMA: Nolan?

521
00:39:38.630 --> 00:39:39.792
Nolan.

522
00:39:49.105 --> 00:39:50.473
Are you still asleep?

523
00:39:52.138 --> 00:39:53.434
Nolan.

524
00:39:53.435 --> 00:39:54.741
There you go.

525
00:39:56.544 --> 00:39:58.580
(SIGHS) You forgot
your bell again.

526
00:39:59.609 --> 00:40:00.912
(BELL JINGLING)

527
00:40:33.347 --> 00:40:35.309
(STREAM BUBBLING SOFTLY)

528
00:41:19.555 --> 00:41:20.555
(SIGHS)

529
00:41:21.524 --> 00:41:22.524
(GRUNTS)

530
00:41:27.696 --> 00:41:28.901
(CROW CAWS)

531
00:41:31.339 --> 00:41:33.301
(UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING)

532
00:41:34.043 --> 00:41:35.171
(CROW CAWS)

533
00:41:39.478 --> 00:41:41.012
(CROW CAWING)

534
00:41:44.515 --> 00:41:45.887
(SQUELCHING)

535
00:41:45.888 --> 00:41:47.216
(CROW CAWS)

536
00:41:53.998 --> 00:41:54.998
(MUSIC SOARS)

537
00:41:56.163 --> 00:41:57.259
(GASPS)

538
00:41:59.894 --> 00:42:01.395
(MUSIC DECREASES)

539
00:42:06.844 --> 00:42:07.844
(GASPS)

540
00:42:09.342 --> 00:42:10.404
(CROW CAWS)

541
00:42:23.251 --> 00:42:25.254
- (CROSSBOW FIRES)
- (MUSIC SOARS)

542
00:42:27.363 --> 00:42:29.225
- (MUSIC FADES)
- (GASPING)

543
00:42:30.792 --> 00:42:32.063
(SCREAMS)

544
00:42:32.563 --> 00:42:33.900
(PANTING)

545
00:42:42.979 --> 00:42:44.410
(GRUNTS)

546
00:42:44.411 --> 00:42:46.583
(DISQUIETING MUSIC PLAYING)

547
00:43:11.933 --> 00:43:13.401
(BARK SNAPPING)

548
00:43:29.293 --> 00:43:31.089
SAMUEL: It's better with sap.

549
00:43:33.293 --> 00:43:34.386
Yeah.

550
00:43:34.387 --> 00:43:36.490
That'll make it taste
less like a tree.

551
00:43:44.102 --> 00:43:46.269
MOMMA: <i>We're doing
the best we can.</i>

552
00:43:47.175 --> 00:43:48.175
Eat.

553
00:44:08.957 --> 00:44:10.293
(MOVEMENT RUSTLES)

554
00:44:26.841 --> 00:44:28.146
Momma?

555
00:44:28.147 --> 00:44:29.147
Sam?

556
00:44:30.011 --> 00:44:31.215
(BELL JINGLES)

557
00:44:35.851 --> 00:44:37.386
(RUSTLING)

558
00:44:39.062 --> 00:44:40.154
(YELPS)

559
00:44:40.155 --> 00:44:42.457
- (SCREAMING)
- (TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

560
00:44:42.458 --> 00:44:46.164
No! (GRUNTING)

561
00:44:46.165 --> 00:44:47.165
No!

562
00:44:48.599 --> 00:44:49.599
No! No!

563
00:44:52.539 --> 00:44:53.539
(MUSIC STOPS)

564
00:44:55.080 --> 00:44:56.108
(BELL JINGLES)

565
00:44:57.741 --> 00:44:59.408
(GASPING)

566
00:45:06.557 --> 00:45:09.121
- (FROG CROAKS)
- (FOOTSTEPS RUSTLE)

567
00:45:23.898 --> 00:45:24.906
Koda.

568
00:45:29.113 --> 00:45:30.439
(DOOR BANGS)

569
00:45:34.648 --> 00:45:36.017
MOMMA: Touch the wood.

570
00:45:36.018 --> 00:45:37.275
Say it!

571
00:45:37.276 --> 00:45:39.379
O blessed house of ancient wood.

572
00:45:39.380 --> 00:45:42.183
(TEARFULLY) Shelter
to the pure and good.

573
00:45:42.184 --> 00:45:44.755
We'll keep you bright
and never roam.

574
00:45:44.756 --> 00:45:47.019
Heaven is here, within our home.

575
00:45:47.020 --> 00:45:48.088
MOMMA: Say it again.

576
00:45:48.089 --> 00:45:50.230
O blessed house of ancient wood.

577
00:45:50.231 --> 00:45:51.464
MOMMA: Again!

578
00:45:51.465 --> 00:45:52.567
NOLAN: O blessed house

579
00:45:52.568 --> 00:45:53.766
- of ancient wood...
- MOMMA: Louder!

580
00:45:53.767 --> 00:45:55.805
NOLAN: Shelter to the pure
and good!

581
00:45:56.503 --> 00:45:57.503
(DOOR SLAMS)

582
00:45:59.934 --> 00:46:01.107
Momma.

583
00:46:07.249 --> 00:46:08.477
Momma!

584
00:46:11.289 --> 00:46:13.317
I have to pee, Momma!

585
00:46:13.948 --> 00:46:15.121
Momma!

586
00:46:31.433 --> 00:46:33.700
Did you feel
the darkness go away?

587
00:46:36.538 --> 00:46:39.475
- (METAL SQUEAKING)
- (CRYPTIC MUSIC PLAYING)

588
00:46:50.558 --> 00:46:51.894
(KODA WHINES)

589
00:46:57.530 --> 00:46:58.530
Sam.

590
00:47:00.161 --> 00:47:01.167
You're awake?

591
00:47:02.800 --> 00:47:04.137
SAMUEL: No.

592
00:47:04.138 --> 00:47:05.402
Sam.

593
00:47:06.704 --> 00:47:07.800
Sam!

594
00:47:09.003 --> 00:47:10.011
Yes.

595
00:47:11.482 --> 00:47:12.882
We need to leave the house.

596
00:47:13.515 --> 00:47:14.675
Goodnight, Nolan.

597
00:47:15.516 --> 00:47:17.351
I'm serious.

598
00:47:17.352 --> 00:47:18.921
- Sam!
- Shh.

599
00:47:24.527 --> 00:47:27.027
How do you wanna leave?

600
00:47:27.028 --> 00:47:29.858
The Evil will catch us as soon
as we take off the rope.

601
00:47:29.859 --> 00:47:30.960
We know the forest.

602
00:47:30.961 --> 00:47:32.491
If we look after each other,

603
00:47:32.492 --> 00:47:34.068
we might have
a chance to outrun it.

604
00:47:34.833 --> 00:47:36.498
What about Momma?

605
00:47:36.499 --> 00:47:38.732
We'll come back for her
once we find something to eat.

606
00:47:40.038 --> 00:47:41.740
Momma knows what's right for us.

607
00:47:41.741 --> 00:47:43.605
I don't think she does anymore.

608
00:47:44.942 --> 00:47:46.314
Did you see her?

609
00:47:46.315 --> 00:47:47.917
She's starving, too.

610
00:47:49.380 --> 00:47:50.980
SAMUEL: She always
figures something out.

611
00:47:52.216 --> 00:47:53.956
NOLAN: For once,
we have to help.

612
00:47:55.416 --> 00:47:57.582
SAMUEL: By disobeying her?

613
00:47:57.583 --> 00:47:59.522
Will you really
let go of the rope?

614
00:48:06.900 --> 00:48:08.102
I can let go of the rope,

615
00:48:09.399 --> 00:48:11.468
but I can't let go
of my brother.

616
00:48:23.817 --> 00:48:25.218
It's too dangerous.

617
00:48:27.148 --> 00:48:28.551
I'm sorry.

618
00:48:32.297 --> 00:48:34.260
(LOUD MUNCHING)

619
00:48:38.730 --> 00:48:39.730
(SNARLS)

620
00:48:43.406 --> 00:48:44.468
(KODA BARKS)

621
00:48:47.510 --> 00:48:48.769
(KODA PANTING)

622
00:49:01.349 --> 00:49:03.322
(GRIM MUSIC PLAYING)

623
00:49:52.742 --> 00:49:54.868
This is a very special tool.

624
00:49:56.547 --> 00:49:57.574
It's called a camera.

625
00:50:00.979 --> 00:50:02.649
What does it do?

626
00:50:02.650 --> 00:50:03.844
MOMMA: Takes pictures.

627
00:50:06.717 --> 00:50:10.488
It captures what it sees,
with this little eye.

628
00:50:13.155 --> 00:50:15.127
You aim it,

629
00:50:15.128 --> 00:50:18.222
then you push this button
right here and...

630
00:50:18.223 --> 00:50:19.233
(WHOOSHES)

631
00:50:20.561 --> 00:50:22.566
A real-life picture comes out.

632
00:50:28.270 --> 00:50:29.408
Like this one.

633
00:50:30.580 --> 00:50:31.608
This was me...

634
00:50:33.078 --> 00:50:34.380
from the old world.

635
00:50:36.280 --> 00:50:38.013
NOLAN: Is that really you?

636
00:50:38.014 --> 00:50:39.418
Hey, hey, careful.

637
00:50:43.388 --> 00:50:45.523
I was a different person
back then.

638
00:50:53.063 --> 00:50:54.070
Or this one.

639
00:50:59.468 --> 00:51:01.308
I took it outside on the porch.

640
00:51:03.413 --> 00:51:04.740
Sam.

641
00:51:08.884 --> 00:51:11.079
- This is us?
- MOMMA: Mm-hmm.

642
00:51:11.080 --> 00:51:12.577
And this is Koda.

643
00:51:12.578 --> 00:51:14.585
- (KODA WHINES)
- MOMMA: Yep.

644
00:51:15.917 --> 00:51:18.526
You can take a picture
of anything you want.

645
00:51:18.527 --> 00:51:20.291
But a good picture

646
00:51:20.292 --> 00:51:22.725
shows more than
what the camera's looking at.

647
00:51:24.592 --> 00:51:26.929
It shows a special moment,

648
00:51:26.930 --> 00:51:28.736
frozen in time.

649
00:51:28.737 --> 00:51:30.667
They can even show a feeling.

650
00:51:31.838 --> 00:51:33.175
Like love.

651
00:51:39.748 --> 00:51:40.748
Where's Poppa?

652
00:51:42.577 --> 00:51:44.642
He was holding the camera.

653
00:51:44.643 --> 00:51:46.287
Do you have a picture of him?

654
00:51:47.149 --> 00:51:49.055
Mm-mm.

655
00:51:49.056 --> 00:51:51.017
These are the only two
I chose to keep.

656
00:51:53.656 --> 00:51:55.893
And there's one more
in there, too.

657
00:51:55.894 --> 00:51:56.894
I've been saving it.

658
00:51:57.534 --> 00:51:58.534
For when?

659
00:52:01.431 --> 00:52:02.699
Look for the right moment.

660
00:52:03.531 --> 00:52:05.467
Maybe you'll find one

661
00:52:05.468 --> 00:52:07.775
that reminds us
what we're living for.

662
00:52:07.776 --> 00:52:09.772
Even if it's something small.

663
00:52:10.982 --> 00:52:13.149
'Cause some moments in life
are hard.

664
00:52:14.645 --> 00:52:18.011
But when we remember
why we're holding on,

665
00:52:18.821 --> 00:52:20.288
we get strong again.

666
00:52:28.962 --> 00:52:30.166
This right here

667
00:52:31.464 --> 00:52:33.796
is about to be
one of those hard moments.

668
00:52:40.305 --> 00:52:42.337
We've been through some brutal,

669
00:52:42.338 --> 00:52:44.437
brutal winters, haven't we?

670
00:52:44.438 --> 00:52:45.874
But nothing like this one.

671
00:52:46.817 --> 00:52:48.009
Everything in the garden,

672
00:52:48.010 --> 00:52:49.141
gone.

673
00:52:50.579 --> 00:52:52.353
The roots are waterlogged.

674
00:52:55.092 --> 00:52:57.083
The animals,
they ain't come back yet.

675
00:52:58.563 --> 00:52:59.657
We got water.

676
00:53:00.424 --> 00:53:02.198
But that'll last us maybe

677
00:53:02.897 --> 00:53:04.290
a couple weeks.

678
00:53:04.291 --> 00:53:05.498
Maybe a month.

679
00:53:10.068 --> 00:53:11.163
But soon...

680
00:53:14.875 --> 00:53:15.937
our bodies

681
00:53:17.210 --> 00:53:18.874
are gonna start shutting down.

682
00:53:23.281 --> 00:53:24.583
And we're gonna die.

683
00:53:33.930 --> 00:53:35.726
So, we only got one option.

684
00:53:40.297 --> 00:53:41.369
And that's Koda.

685
00:53:42.363 --> 00:53:43.497
What?

686
00:53:43.498 --> 00:53:45.369
MOMMA: We can salt the meat.

687
00:53:45.370 --> 00:53:47.039
Maybe it'll last us
a month or so

688
00:53:47.040 --> 00:53:49.036
- before it's spoiled.
- No!

689
00:53:51.474 --> 00:53:52.612
I know you love him.

690
00:53:52.613 --> 00:53:53.773
We all do.

691
00:53:53.774 --> 00:53:55.711
But he nearing
the end of his life,

692
00:53:55.712 --> 00:53:58.346
and he... he ain't caught us
nothing in months.

693
00:53:58.347 --> 00:53:59.678
We can eat more frogs.

694
00:53:59.679 --> 00:54:01.449
That's not gonna be enough.

695
00:54:01.450 --> 00:54:02.549
I'll eat the bark, the bugs.

696
00:54:02.550 --> 00:54:03.749
I don't mind it, Momma. I swear.

697
00:54:03.750 --> 00:54:05.058
- Nolan.
- Maybe it's safe to leave.

698
00:54:05.059 --> 00:54:06.688
I was out there
without a rope on.

699
00:54:06.689 --> 00:54:08.258
The Evil coulda touched me,
but it didn't.

700
00:54:08.259 --> 00:54:09.921
MOMMA: 'Cause it chose not to.

701
00:54:09.922 --> 00:54:11.927
It wants you to doubt me.
And look...

702
00:54:13.136 --> 00:54:14.699
that's exactly
what you're doing.

703
00:54:14.700 --> 00:54:16.902
What if you're wrong? What if
the world is still out there?

704
00:54:16.903 --> 00:54:18.531
This is the world!

705
00:54:18.532 --> 00:54:20.306
There's nothing out there!

706
00:54:20.307 --> 00:54:23.040
It's either the house
or the Evil. That's it!

707
00:54:23.041 --> 00:54:24.570
No. This is evil.

708
00:54:24.571 --> 00:54:26.810
Eating family is evil!

709
00:54:26.811 --> 00:54:29.573
If we can't feed ourselves,
how are we gonna feed the dog?

710
00:54:29.574 --> 00:54:30.978
You wanna die?

711
00:54:30.979 --> 00:54:33.920
I don't wanna die, but I don't
wanna see my friend die!

712
00:54:33.921 --> 00:54:35.582
But this is not fair!

713
00:54:35.583 --> 00:54:37.821
All he's done is protect us!

714
00:54:40.797 --> 00:54:41.825
Let's ask Samuel.

715
00:54:43.758 --> 00:54:44.997
Of course he'll do what you say.

716
00:54:44.998 --> 00:54:47.028
He can talk for hisself.

717
00:54:49.540 --> 00:54:50.540
Samuel?

718
00:54:56.339 --> 00:54:57.769
We have to.

719
00:54:57.770 --> 00:54:59.740
I hate you! I hate both of you.

720
00:54:59.741 --> 00:55:02.109
I hate this house!
I hate this house!

721
00:55:03.449 --> 00:55:04.881
- Come on, Koda.
- (KODA WHINES)

722
00:55:09.891 --> 00:55:10.986
(DOOR SHUTS)

723
00:55:12.556 --> 00:55:15.287
Momma, I can do it if you want.

724
00:55:19.460 --> 00:55:21.031
No.

725
00:55:21.032 --> 00:55:22.404
(DOOR OPENS)

726
00:55:24.468 --> 00:55:26.034
(FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING)

727
00:55:27.140 --> 00:55:28.509
(KODA WHINES)

728
00:55:33.717 --> 00:55:34.717
NOLAN: No.

729
00:55:37.019 --> 00:55:38.443
- No!
- (KODA WHINING)

730
00:55:38.444 --> 00:55:40.149
No. No!

731
00:55:40.150 --> 00:55:43.047
No! No! No!

732
00:55:43.048 --> 00:55:45.626
- (WOEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)
- Koda! Koda!

733
00:55:45.627 --> 00:55:46.824
No! (SOBS)

734
00:55:47.589 --> 00:55:49.796
No! Momma, please!

735
00:55:49.797 --> 00:55:51.324
Please, no!

736
00:55:51.325 --> 00:55:52.566
Koda!

737
00:55:54.528 --> 00:55:55.668
Koda!

738
00:55:56.365 --> 00:55:57.373
Please!

739
00:55:58.874 --> 00:55:59.874
(WHIMPERS)

740
00:56:03.505 --> 00:56:04.776
(PANTING)

741
00:56:14.123 --> 00:56:15.457
MOMMA: You're a good dog.

742
00:56:16.221 --> 00:56:17.588
I thank you

743
00:56:17.589 --> 00:56:20.220
- for taking good care of us.
- (KODA WHIMPERS)

744
00:56:25.636 --> 00:56:27.029
(CRYING)

745
00:56:28.729 --> 00:56:29.933
(KODA WHIMPERS)

746
00:56:35.036 --> 00:56:37.446
(VOICE BREAKS)
You're a good dog.

747
00:56:41.918 --> 00:56:42.918
(CROSSBOW CREAKS)

748
00:56:55.997 --> 00:56:57.323
(PANTING)

749
00:57:12.006 --> 00:57:13.581
- (KODA WHINING)
- (STIFLES SOB)

750
00:57:18.019 --> 00:57:19.019
(EXHALES)

751
00:57:20.858 --> 00:57:22.249
(KODA WHINES)

752
00:57:23.092 --> 00:57:25.021
(TENSE MUSIC BUILDING)

753
00:57:27.296 --> 00:57:28.860
- NOLAN: Momma.
- (MUSIC FADES)

754
00:57:31.495 --> 00:57:32.624
MOMMA: Nolan.

755
00:57:32.625 --> 00:57:33.634
It's not real.

756
00:57:34.300 --> 00:57:35.636
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

757
00:57:36.302 --> 00:57:37.302
Listen to me.

758
00:57:40.944 --> 00:57:42.739
You need to see.

759
00:57:42.740 --> 00:57:45.612
You need to see there's
nothing to be scared of!

760
00:57:45.613 --> 00:57:47.738
That's what it wants you
to think, baby. Don't do it!

761
00:57:47.739 --> 00:57:49.310
No! Don't do it.

762
00:57:49.311 --> 00:57:51.117
No. No.

763
00:57:51.118 --> 00:57:53.317
Nolan! Open this door.

764
00:57:53.318 --> 00:57:54.318
- (DOOR BANGS)
- Nolan!

765
00:57:56.322 --> 00:57:57.585
Open the door.

766
00:57:57.586 --> 00:57:59.187
- Nolan!
- (DOOR BANGING)

767
00:58:01.361 --> 00:58:04.290
Nolan, I... I lied.

768
00:58:04.291 --> 00:58:07.429
I didn't tell you everything.
I brought the Evil here.

769
00:58:07.430 --> 00:58:09.195
The Evil is real!

770
00:58:09.196 --> 00:58:11.930
And if it touches me
and gets inside the house,

771
00:58:11.931 --> 00:58:14.097
it's gonna make me kill you!

772
00:58:14.098 --> 00:58:15.467
- Open the door.
- (DOOR BANGS)

773
00:58:16.241 --> 00:58:17.304
Please!

774
00:58:18.147 --> 00:58:19.977
Open the fucking door!

775
00:58:24.417 --> 00:58:25.686
- Nolan!
- (SAMUEL YELLS)

776
00:58:26.385 --> 00:58:27.385
NOLAN: Momma!

777
00:58:30.092 --> 00:58:31.824
(BOTH GRUNTING)

778
00:58:38.533 --> 00:58:40.327
GRANDMA: (DISTORTED)
Bad little goat.

779
00:58:42.399 --> 00:58:43.497
(GASPS)

780
00:58:43.498 --> 00:58:45.637
Bad little goat.

781
00:58:45.638 --> 00:58:49.472
Bad little goat,
caught sitting in my chair.

782
00:58:49.473 --> 00:58:51.540
(CLAPPING RHYTHMICALLY)

783
00:58:51.541 --> 00:58:53.172
Let's see that tushy,

784
00:58:53.173 --> 00:58:56.080
and I'll make it
so you can't sit anywhere.

785
00:58:56.081 --> 00:58:57.382
It's here!

786
00:58:57.383 --> 00:58:58.884
- (BOTH GRUNT)
- It's here!

787
00:58:59.616 --> 00:59:01.221
SAMUEL: Momma!

788
00:59:01.222 --> 00:59:03.322
- (GRUNTS)
- (SAMUEL GROANS)

789
00:59:03.323 --> 00:59:04.650
SAMUEL: Damn it. What the hell?

790
00:59:04.651 --> 00:59:06.023
(WHIMPERING)

791
00:59:06.722 --> 00:59:08.025
(BLEATING) Bad!

792
00:59:08.458 --> 00:59:11.729
Bad!

793
00:59:11.730 --> 00:59:16.572
Bad little goat,
putting poison in my food.

794
00:59:17.205 --> 00:59:19.201
Bad little goat.

795
00:59:19.810 --> 00:59:21.533
Bad!

796
00:59:22.869 --> 00:59:24.201
I told you,

797
00:59:24.202 --> 00:59:27.374
I'm gonna make you
eat your babies.

798
00:59:29.977 --> 00:59:31.719
You'll never get in.

799
00:59:33.483 --> 00:59:34.656
No!

800
00:59:42.130 --> 00:59:43.425
(CHOKING)

801
00:59:43.426 --> 00:59:45.022
(BOTH GRUNTING)

802
00:59:45.023 --> 00:59:46.998
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

803
00:59:53.505 --> 00:59:54.505
SAMUEL: Momma!

804
00:59:56.136 --> 00:59:58.075
- (MUSIC STOPS)
- (GASPING)

805
00:59:59.916 --> 01:00:00.916
Momma?

806
01:00:02.316 --> 01:00:03.808
Wake up, Momma.

807
01:00:03.809 --> 01:00:05.115
Momma, wake up!

808
01:00:11.794 --> 01:00:13.926
It's okay, Momma.
I'm tying the ropes together.

809
01:00:16.794 --> 01:00:18.029
It's okay, Momma. It's okay.

810
01:00:18.695 --> 01:00:19.866
Momma, please.

811
01:00:24.365 --> 01:00:26.768
(QUIVERING) O blessed house
of ancient wood.

812
01:00:26.769 --> 01:00:29.509
Shelter to the pure and good.

813
01:00:29.510 --> 01:00:33.104
We'll keep you bright
and never roam.

814
01:00:33.105 --> 01:00:35.508
Heaven is here, within our home.

815
01:00:36.945 --> 01:00:38.117
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

816
01:00:38.118 --> 01:00:40.485
Momma, please.

817
01:00:40.486 --> 01:00:42.456
The house has us now, Momma.

818
01:00:42.457 --> 01:00:45.320
You can wake up.
Please, Momma, wake up.

819
01:00:46.361 --> 01:00:47.588
(TEARFULLY) I need you.

820
01:00:47.589 --> 01:00:49.292
Please, Momma.

821
01:00:49.293 --> 01:00:50.791
(CRYING)

822
01:00:50.792 --> 01:00:53.267
(MOURNFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

823
01:00:53.268 --> 01:00:55.764
O blessed house of ancient wood.

824
01:00:55.765 --> 01:00:58.538
Shelter to the pure and good.

825
01:00:58.539 --> 01:01:01.440
We'll keep you bright
and never roam.

826
01:01:01.441 --> 01:01:03.371
Heaven is here, within our home.

827
01:01:04.741 --> 01:01:06.715
Momma, please.

828
01:01:09.185 --> 01:01:10.543
Please, Momma.

829
01:01:12.520 --> 01:01:14.481
(SAMUEL CONTINUES CRYING)

830
01:01:42.212 --> 01:01:44.753
<i>(OUR LOVE</i>
BY STARR SISTERS PLAYING)

831
01:01:49.391 --> 01:01:52.919
<i>♪ Our love ♪</i>

832
01:01:52.920 --> 01:01:56.990
<i>♪ Is like a song ♪</i>

833
01:01:56.991 --> 01:02:00.733
<i>♪ That lingers on ♪</i>

834
01:02:00.734 --> 01:02:05.032
<i>♪ With it
light-hearted laughter ♪</i>

835
01:02:05.033 --> 01:02:09.870
<i>♪ Leaving tears ever after ♪</i>

836
01:02:09.871 --> 01:02:14.538
<i>♪ Fading away ♪</i>

837
01:02:14.539 --> 01:02:21.587
<i>♪ The night
is like a symphony ♪</i>

838
01:02:21.588 --> 01:02:25.722
<i>♪ But there's no melody ♪</i>

839
01:02:25.723 --> 01:02:29.223
<i>♪ Without your love ♪</i>

840
01:02:29.224 --> 01:02:31.096
- (SONG FADES OUT)
- (CLOCK STOPS TICKING)

841
01:02:40.340 --> 01:02:41.733
Koda!

842
01:02:45.972 --> 01:02:47.574
Koda!

843
01:02:48.008 --> 01:02:49.411
(PANTING)

844
01:02:52.179 --> 01:02:53.580
(IN DISTANCE) Koda!

845
01:02:54.354 --> 01:02:55.653
Koda!

846
01:02:55.654 --> 01:02:57.452
- Come back!
- (KODA WHINES)

847
01:02:57.984 --> 01:02:59.557
Koda!

848
01:02:59.558 --> 01:03:01.687
(FORLORN MUSIC PLAYING)

849
01:03:09.129 --> 01:03:10.129
(FIRE STARTS)

850
01:03:10.668 --> 01:03:11.939
(BLOWING)

851
01:03:42.800 --> 01:03:44.070
(DOOR CREAKS)

852
01:03:45.706 --> 01:03:48.266
I made some pine needle tea.

853
01:03:48.267 --> 01:03:49.801
It'll help with your hunger.

854
01:03:52.646 --> 01:03:54.179
Was that you out there?

855
01:03:57.386 --> 01:03:58.513
NOLAN: Out where?

856
01:04:00.982 --> 01:04:02.220
I saw you,

857
01:04:03.425 --> 01:04:05.682
in the woods,

858
01:04:05.683 --> 01:04:08.721
laughing at me for not
being able to save her.

859
01:04:12.097 --> 01:04:13.759
NOLAN: I think
you were dreaming.

860
01:04:17.571 --> 01:04:18.874
Touch the wood.

861
01:04:22.707 --> 01:04:23.707
Touch it.

862
01:04:30.718 --> 01:04:34.015
O blessed house of ancient wood.

863
01:04:34.016 --> 01:04:36.921
Shelter to the pure and good.

864
01:04:36.922 --> 01:04:40.252
We'll keep you bright
and never roam.

865
01:04:40.253 --> 01:04:42.854
Heaven is here, within our home.

866
01:04:51.207 --> 01:04:52.207
Okay.

867
01:04:52.737 --> 01:04:53.737
Now drink.

868
01:04:56.940 --> 01:04:58.144
You need some air.

869
01:05:01.647 --> 01:05:03.050
(GROANING)

870
01:05:06.621 --> 01:05:08.385
I won't let you die.

871
01:05:26.641 --> 01:05:28.603
(DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING)

872
01:05:44.988 --> 01:05:46.357
(CROW CAWING)

873
01:05:55.296 --> 01:05:57.533
(DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES)

874
01:06:21.990 --> 01:06:23.064
(GRUNTS)

875
01:06:37.403 --> 01:06:38.673
(MUSIC FADES OUT)

876
01:06:41.009 --> 01:06:42.009
(GRUNTS)

877
01:06:55.993 --> 01:06:57.395
(WIND BLOWING)

878
01:07:01.700 --> 01:07:03.104
Help!

879
01:07:04.505 --> 01:07:05.931
Help!

880
01:07:08.707 --> 01:07:10.045
Hello!

881
01:07:14.010 --> 01:07:15.512
(GRUNTING)

882
01:07:22.215 --> 01:07:23.784
Help!

883
01:07:31.261 --> 01:07:33.464
(SOFT SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

884
01:07:40.476 --> 01:07:41.703
Excuse me!

885
01:07:43.105 --> 01:07:44.277
Hi, there.

886
01:07:45.275 --> 01:07:47.247
Sorry to intrude. I just, uh...

887
01:07:48.046 --> 01:07:50.281
I was hiking, and I...

888
01:07:50.282 --> 01:07:52.545
I thought I heard someone
screaming for help.

889
01:07:52.546 --> 01:07:54.551
That wasn't you,
by any chance, was it?

890
01:07:55.987 --> 01:07:57.221
I... (CHUCKLES)

891
01:07:57.222 --> 01:07:59.590
I thought my ears
were playing tricks on me.

892
01:07:59.591 --> 01:08:00.788
(CHUCKLES)

893
01:08:02.493 --> 01:08:04.354
Wow, I didn't think
anyone was out here.

894
01:08:04.355 --> 01:08:05.595
This is, uh...

895
01:08:07.832 --> 01:08:08.832
Ah.

896
01:08:15.138 --> 01:08:16.138
Are you okay?

897
01:08:20.947 --> 01:08:22.480
What's your name, son?

898
01:08:24.180 --> 01:08:25.450
(SOFTLY) Nolan.

899
01:08:26.953 --> 01:08:28.084
(UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING)

900
01:08:28.085 --> 01:08:29.355
I'm sorry, I didn't catch that.

901
01:08:30.186 --> 01:08:31.654
- Nolan.
- Nolan.

902
01:08:33.025 --> 01:08:34.492
Hi, Nolan. I'm Cole.

903
01:08:35.929 --> 01:08:37.088
It's nice to meet you.

904
01:08:38.127 --> 01:08:39.127
So, uh...

905
01:08:41.102 --> 01:08:43.303
Where your folks at?
They around?

906
01:08:45.432 --> 01:08:47.136
My momma's dead.

907
01:08:47.137 --> 01:08:49.034
Oh, I'm very sorry to hear that.

908
01:08:51.372 --> 01:08:52.708
How did she pass?

909
01:08:54.016 --> 01:08:56.340
My brother's sick.
He needs food.

910
01:08:56.341 --> 01:08:57.445
COLE: Okay.

911
01:08:57.446 --> 01:08:59.715
Well, I've got some food
in my pack.

912
01:09:01.623 --> 01:09:03.289
You know,

913
01:09:03.290 --> 01:09:05.986
Nolan, I've got a truck
about five miles from here,

914
01:09:05.987 --> 01:09:07.853
- and I could take you and your brother...
- SAMUEL: Get back!

915
01:09:07.854 --> 01:09:10.661
COLE: Whoa. Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Okay. Okay, okay.

916
01:09:10.662 --> 01:09:11.662
Whoa.

917
01:09:12.028 --> 01:09:13.028
Okay.

918
01:09:13.403 --> 01:09:14.462
Uh...

919
01:09:14.463 --> 01:09:17.100
Look, I don't mean
you boys any harm.

920
01:09:17.101 --> 01:09:18.866
Nolan here says you're sick.

921
01:09:19.842 --> 01:09:22.008
- We're not stupid.
- Sam.

922
01:09:22.009 --> 01:09:24.969
I didn't say
you were stupid. I just...

923
01:09:24.970 --> 01:09:27.680
I just thought someone
was in trouble. That's it.

924
01:09:27.681 --> 01:09:28.945
You killed my momma.

925
01:09:28.946 --> 01:09:30.179
COLE: No, son. I...

926
01:09:30.180 --> 01:09:32.448
I don't know your momma. Okay?

927
01:09:32.449 --> 01:09:34.483
Look, this was just...
this was a mistake.

928
01:09:34.484 --> 01:09:36.152
I'm sorry. I'm gonna go.
I'm gonna leave now,

929
01:09:36.153 --> 01:09:37.285
- all right?
- Don't move.

930
01:09:37.286 --> 01:09:40.651
I ju... Okay. Just calm down.

931
01:09:40.652 --> 01:09:42.056
What if he's a real person?

932
01:09:42.057 --> 01:09:43.264
We were happy.

933
01:09:45.768 --> 01:09:48.024
Listen to me, okay?

934
01:09:48.025 --> 01:09:50.336
I'm just gonna turn,
I'm just gonna go back.

935
01:09:50.337 --> 01:09:52.465
I'm gonna go back from where
I came from, all right?

936
01:09:52.466 --> 01:09:54.740
- Just...
- I said, "Don't move!"

937
01:09:54.741 --> 01:09:56.277
(BREATHES ANXIOUSLY)

938
01:09:57.505 --> 01:09:59.739
Look, everything's fine.

939
01:09:59.740 --> 01:10:01.540
- NOLAN: Just let him go.
- Everything's okay.

940
01:10:02.179 --> 01:10:03.383
Let him go, Sam.

941
01:10:06.214 --> 01:10:07.214
Please.

942
01:10:08.382 --> 01:10:09.382
It's over.

943
01:10:10.692 --> 01:10:11.692
She's gone.

944
01:10:15.630 --> 01:10:16.792
No!

945
01:10:19.228 --> 01:10:20.392
(GROANING)

946
01:10:20.393 --> 01:10:21.566
- (PANTING)
- Sam...

947
01:10:23.905 --> 01:10:25.966
(CONTINUES GROANING)

948
01:10:30.911 --> 01:10:32.379
COLE: Help me!

949
01:10:32.978 --> 01:10:34.272
(COLE YELLS)

950
01:10:34.273 --> 01:10:35.943
Help me!

951
01:10:39.282 --> 01:10:40.416
Nolan, don't.

952
01:10:40.417 --> 01:10:42.589
- He said he has food.
- It's a trick.

953
01:10:42.590 --> 01:10:44.124
COLE: Help me!

954
01:10:44.125 --> 01:10:46.756
- (SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)
- (NOLAN PANTING)

955
01:11:16.123 --> 01:11:17.820
(COLE GRUNTING STRAINFULLY)

956
01:11:21.797 --> 01:11:23.661
(COUGHS, GURGLES)

957
01:11:24.426 --> 01:11:26.092
(COUGHS, GROANING)

958
01:11:33.301 --> 01:11:34.301
(GASPS)

959
01:11:35.372 --> 01:11:37.567
(CHOKING AND STRAINING)

960
01:11:37.568 --> 01:11:39.171
(LINE RINGING)

961
01:11:44.682 --> 01:11:46.202
DISPATCHER: <i>911.
What's your emergency?</i>

962
01:11:48.218 --> 01:11:49.446
(GROANING)

963
01:11:49.447 --> 01:11:50.457
<i>Sir?</i>

964
01:11:51.322 --> 01:11:52.789
<i>Sir, can you hear me?</i>

965
01:11:53.863 --> 01:11:55.089
<i>Can you tell me...</i>

966
01:11:55.090 --> 01:11:56.619
(GASPS)

967
01:11:56.620 --> 01:11:58.058
(BOTH GRUNTING)

968
01:11:59.132 --> 01:12:00.962
<i>Sir...</i> (INDISTINCT)

969
01:12:02.838 --> 01:12:04.471
(BOTH STRAINING)

970
01:12:08.838 --> 01:12:10.741
<i>- Sir, tell me where you are.</i>
- (GURGLES)

971
01:12:30.930 --> 01:12:31.930
Huh.

972
01:12:37.597 --> 01:12:38.835
(GRUNTING)

973
01:12:42.602 --> 01:12:43.741
(EXHALES)

974
01:12:50.917 --> 01:12:51.983
Mm.

975
01:12:51.984 --> 01:12:53.586
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

976
01:12:56.716 --> 01:12:58.283
(DOOR CREAKS)

977
01:13:07.364 --> 01:13:08.535
It's from the man.

978
01:13:10.872 --> 01:13:12.033
He's dead.

979
01:13:14.910 --> 01:13:16.807
That wasn't a man.

980
01:13:18.142 --> 01:13:19.142
Try it.

981
01:13:20.146 --> 01:13:21.273
Did you let go?

982
01:13:22.146 --> 01:13:23.146
No.

983
01:13:24.218 --> 01:13:25.748
I touched him with the rope on.

984
01:13:25.749 --> 01:13:28.148
He wouldn't have let me
if he was the Evil, right?

985
01:13:29.387 --> 01:13:31.389
You still won't learn.

986
01:13:31.390 --> 01:13:33.791
You're falling for it
all over again!

987
01:13:34.555 --> 01:13:35.826
Just try it.

988
01:13:40.329 --> 01:13:41.935
No.

989
01:13:41.936 --> 01:13:44.530
Maybe there's no Evil.

990
01:13:44.531 --> 01:13:45.935
Momma lied to us.

991
01:13:47.772 --> 01:13:50.641
We're not the only ones left
in the world.

992
01:13:50.642 --> 01:13:52.375
If we thought there was
nothing out there for us,

993
01:13:52.376 --> 01:13:53.806
then we wouldn't
wanna leave her.

994
01:13:53.807 --> 01:13:55.444
She killed herself
to keep us safe,

995
01:13:55.445 --> 01:13:57.113
and you still won't believe it!

996
01:13:57.114 --> 01:13:58.486
Just try it!

997
01:14:00.617 --> 01:14:02.248
You'll see that it's real!

998
01:14:03.323 --> 01:14:05.526
It'll make you feel better!

999
01:14:08.490 --> 01:14:09.662
I promise.

1000
01:14:12.462 --> 01:14:13.795
Once upon a time,

1001
01:14:13.796 --> 01:14:15.835
there were two brothers
who trusted each other.

1002
01:14:15.836 --> 01:14:17.428
She loved you!

1003
01:14:18.798 --> 01:14:20.332
She loved you.

1004
01:14:21.836 --> 01:14:23.940
And I'm so sorry for what I did.

1005
01:14:28.611 --> 01:14:29.979
But we're not safe.

1006
01:14:33.119 --> 01:14:35.421
We're dying.

1007
01:14:35.422 --> 01:14:37.448
At least then we'll be
with Momma again.

1008
01:14:38.889 --> 01:14:41.122
Maybe that'll be enough
for you this time.

1009
01:14:47.631 --> 01:14:49.801
(DISQUIETING MUSIC PLAYING)

1010
01:14:54.405 --> 01:14:55.906
(WIND WHISTLING)

1011
01:15:55.401 --> 01:15:57.396
(PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING)

1012
01:16:21.129 --> 01:16:22.993
(CHAIR CREAKING)

1013
01:16:40.249 --> 01:16:42.078
- (OBJECT RATTLES)
- (GASPS)

1014
01:17:03.798 --> 01:17:04.798
SAMUEL: Hello?

1015
01:17:08.440 --> 01:17:09.644
Who's in there?

1016
01:17:10.946 --> 01:17:11.946
Koda?

1017
01:17:18.052 --> 01:17:19.052
Hello?

1018
01:17:19.680 --> 01:17:20.680
(WHOOSH)

1019
01:17:34.635 --> 01:17:36.869
- (DRAMATIC NOTE PLAYS)
- (SAMUEL SHOUTS)

1020
01:17:37.368 --> 01:17:38.368
Momma?

1021
01:17:41.075 --> 01:17:42.075
(GROANS)

1022
01:17:48.216 --> 01:17:49.508
(FLIES BUZZING)

1023
01:17:53.651 --> 01:17:55.316
- Hello?
- (SAMUEL GASPS)

1024
01:17:58.854 --> 01:18:00.827
I'm looking for my dad.

1025
01:18:02.430 --> 01:18:03.988
He asked me to wait by the car,

1026
01:18:03.989 --> 01:18:05.161
but he never came back.

1027
01:18:09.503 --> 01:18:11.101
Do you mind lowering that?

1028
01:18:16.176 --> 01:18:17.176
Thanks.

1029
01:18:18.511 --> 01:18:20.044
How did you get here?

1030
01:18:22.078 --> 01:18:24.213
I followed his footsteps
in the mud.

1031
01:18:25.788 --> 01:18:29.185
He's tall, black hair,
a bit of gray on the sides?

1032
01:18:30.885 --> 01:18:32.089
Have you seen him?

1033
01:18:39.766 --> 01:18:41.802
Why is that rope
around your waist?

1034
01:18:44.701 --> 01:18:46.136
To keep me safe.

1035
01:18:46.966 --> 01:18:48.072
From what?

1036
01:18:54.440 --> 01:18:56.278
Where did you get
that flashlight?

1037
01:18:59.650 --> 01:19:00.887
That's my dad's.

1038
01:19:02.257 --> 01:19:03.791
It was a mistake.

1039
01:19:05.117 --> 01:19:06.755
I didn't mean to.

1040
01:19:06.756 --> 01:19:07.927
What are you talking about?

1041
01:19:08.658 --> 01:19:09.797
Where is he?

1042
01:19:14.500 --> 01:19:15.730
What did you do?

1043
01:19:15.731 --> 01:19:17.464
What did you do to him?

1044
01:19:18.904 --> 01:19:20.500
SAMUEL: I thought
he was the Evil.

1045
01:19:22.144 --> 01:19:23.239
No, wait!

1046
01:19:27.108 --> 01:19:29.179
I thought he was the Evil!

1047
01:19:30.317 --> 01:19:31.977
Come back!

1048
01:19:31.978 --> 01:19:33.986
(TENSE MUSIC PLAYING)

1049
01:19:44.858 --> 01:19:45.858
(GRUNTS)

1050
01:19:46.927 --> 01:19:47.927
Come back!

1051
01:19:54.101 --> 01:19:56.140
The rope... Oh, no.

1052
01:20:03.648 --> 01:20:05.250
Please! Come back!

1053
01:20:05.251 --> 01:20:06.645
(STRAINING)

1054
01:20:11.721 --> 01:20:13.058
